Brief done. The fix: `siblingTable` compared only names **every** member exported, so one odd member emptied the whole table. Now members are grouped by the exported callable they share (≥2 members per group), each group is compared positionally as before, and members that join no group become `unclear` rows over their own exported declarations plus a limit naming them.

Changed only `src/siblings.ts` and `src/commands.ts`; two lines appended to `nodes/a1r3-build-opencode.progress.md`.

Last lines of each check:

```
bun test:  381 pass  0 fail  (16485 expect() calls) — Ran 381 tests across 19 files. [120.27s]
bunx tsgo --noEmit: (no output) exit 0
eval: Requirements: {"MET":8,"NOT MET":0,"NOT CHECKED":2}   Fails-if lines: {"MET":18,"NOT MET":0,"NOT CHECKED":2}   Cases: {"MET":70,"NOT MET":0,"NOT CHECKED":0}
      report.md: | A1 | MET | (A6 and L2 remain NOT CHECKED, as in the pre-change baseline)
```

The mixed table now reads: `shared` on the four plugins' `FileAccess`, `varies` on the writers' `Permission`, plus `unclear` rows for `plugins/defaults.ts` and `plugins/helpers.ts` citing their own exports, and the limit `not compared with the other siblings, because no other member exports the same callables: plugins/defaults.ts, plugins/helpers.ts`.
